course: dictionary
lesson: 6699
title: Oct: short for October, or eight
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Oct» is an abbreviation, a short way of writing a longer word. Most often it is short for October, the tenth month of the year. You see it on calendars, dates and forms, like «12 Oct 2025».
explain: Why does October sound like eight? The prefix «oct-» means eight, as in octopus (eight arms) and octagon (eight sides). In the old Roman calendar the year began in March, so October was the eighth month, and the name stayed even after the months moved.
explain: «Oct» has two other meanings in other subjects. In music, an octave is the gap from one note to the next note with the same name, which is 8 notes. In computing and maths, oct can mean octal, counting in base 8. Look at the subject around the word to know which meaning fits.
fact: «Oct» is an abbreviation, a short form of a longer word.
fact: «Oct» means October, the tenth month of the year.
fact: The prefix «oct-» means eight, as in octopus and octagon.
fact: In music, an octave is 8 notes apart, from one note to the next with the same name.
fact: In the old Roman calendar, «October (oct = 8)» was the eighth month, so its name comes from eight.
exercise: What does «Oct» mean on a date such as «12 Oct 2025»? | Octave | Octagon | * October, the tenth month | Octopus
exercise: The prefix «oct-» means eight. Which word has eight sides? | Octopus | Octave | * Octagon | October
exercise: In music, an octave is the gap from one note to the next note with the same name. How many notes is that? | 7 | 5 | * 8 | 12
test: In the old Roman calendar, «October (oct = 8)» was the eighth month. Why is its name so close to eight? | * Because oct- means eight | Because the Romans liked the number eight | Because October has eight days | Because it was the eighth day of the week
test: Which subject uses «oct» to mean base 8? | * Computing and maths | Geography | Music | Cooking
exam: A form asks, «Date of birth: 4 Oct». What month is it? | Octal | * October, the tenth month | Octopus | Octave
